{ A module with state and a postlude, for module-activation.a68: every
  activation prints a line and starts with count 0, the postlude prints
  the count it ends with. set is an identity declaration, so a call of it
  goes through the procedure value instead of a typed entry. }
module Activation =
def
    pub int count := 0;
    pub proc show = void: puts ("count " + whole (count, 0) + "'n");
    pub proc bump = void: count +:= 1;
    pub proc (int) void set = (int n) void: count := n;
    puts ("activated'n")
postlude
    puts ("revoked with count " + whole (count, 0) + "'n")
fed
